[
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_001",
    "text": "**NovaCore Technologies Pvt. Ltd.  \nREMOTE WORK POLICY**\n\n| **Document ID**      | HR-POL-002                    |\n|----------------------|-------------------------------|\n| **Department**       | HR                            |\n| **Document Type**    | Policy                        |\n| **Policy Title**     | Hybrid and Remote Work Policy |\n| **Version**          | 2026                          |\n| **Effective Date**   | 01-Apr-2026                   |\n| **Owner Department** | HR                            |",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "Document Introduction",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_001"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_002",
    "text": "This policy defines eligibility, approval, working arrangements, attendance, equipment, security, and responsibilities for hybrid and remote work.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "1. Purpose",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_002"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_003",
    "text": "This policy applies to employees whose roles and business requirements permit remote or hybrid work.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "2. Scope",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_003"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_004",
    "text": "Eligible employees may work remotely up to 2 days per week, subject to manager approval, role requirements, team coordination, and business needs.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "3. Eligibility",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_004"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_005",
    "text": "Remote work may be used as part of an approved hybrid arrangement. Employees are expected to maintain agreed working hours, availability, communication, and performance standards.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "4. Work Arrangements",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_005"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_006",
    "text": "Employees must obtain manager approval for planned remote-work days. Managers may decline or modify remote-work arrangements where business requirements, collaboration needs, customer commitments, or operational conditions require on-site presence.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "5. Approval",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_006"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_007",
    "text": "This policy does not define a final approving authority for permanent fully remote arrangements. Such arrangements therefore require separate organizational guidance or approval outside the definitive rules stated in this document.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "6. Permanent Fully Remote Arrangements",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_007"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_008",
    "text": "Employees working remotely must remain available during agreed working hours and follow attendance and meeting requirements.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "7. Working Hours and Attendance",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_008"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_009",
    "text": "Employees must maintain a suitable work environment and use company-approved devices and equipment where required.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "8. Workspace and Equipment",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_009"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_010",
    "text": "Remote work must use company-approved devices, secure authentication, approved network/security controls, and other requirements defined by IT Security Policy and IT Standards.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "9. Information Security",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_010"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_011",
    "text": "Employees maintain availability, security, and work standards. Managers evaluate business suitability and approve routine remote-work days. HR maintains policy guidance. IT defines and supports applicable technical security controls.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "10. Responsibilities",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_011"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_012",
    "text": "Exceptions may be considered for documented business or employee circumstances. Permanent arrangements are not governed by a final authority in this policy.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/HR/Remote_Work_Policy.docx",
      "policy_title": "Hybrid and Remote Work Policy",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "HR",
      "document_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY",
      "section": "11. Exceptions",
      "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_012"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "HR_REMOTE_WORK_POLICY_CHUNK_013",
    "text": "2025 — Initial hybrid work guidance issued. 2026 — Remote-work eligibility, security requirements, and exception handling updated.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "HR",
      "document_name": "Remote_Work_Policy",
